{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789867519,"nonce":"tK0HjcKIDMk4t92Gl+j5h22xh0w=","message":"Decided 2026-09-19: (b), the iteration entity, as this issue's own second comment leaned. Its own namespace refs/iterations, ops Create/SetDates/SetCapacity/SetState, referenced from issues by a cardinality-1 relation of kind `iteration`, mapped to Jira sprints and Linear cycles.\n\nImplementation split out into 87a48c1, which did not exist — this issue only decided the shape.\n\nThe consequence worth writing down: closing an iteration is not atomic. Marking it closed plus moving N unfinished issues is N+1 commits. Ordering makes a crash recoverable: create the next iteration, move the issues, then close the old one, so the intermediate state reads as 'some issues already moved' and retry is idempotent. Closing first would strand issues in a closed iteration.\n\nSee doc/design/configurable-schema.md, D5.","files":null}]}